ack command — parse payload and dispatch to attack handler |\\n| `> 0x0000` | Attack command — parse payload and dispatch |\\n\\n#### Attack Command Payload Structure\\n\\nWhen command type is non-zero, the payload contains attack parameters:\\n\\n```\\n+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+\\n| Targets | Method | Duration | Num Targets | Num Options | ...   |\\n| (4 bytes)| (1 byte)| (4 bytes)| (1 byte) | (1 byte) | ...   |\\n| Network | ID     | Seconds  |            |            | ...   |\\n| Byte    |        |          |            |            | ...   |\\n| Order   |        |          |            |            | ...   |\\n+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+\\n Offset 0   Offset 4  Offset 5   Offset 6    Offset 7\\n```\\n\\n**Payload Fields:**\\n\\n| Field | Offset | Size | Encoding | Description |\\n|-------|--------|------|----------|-------------|\\n| Duration | 0 | 4 bytes | Network byte order uint32 | Attack duration in seconds |\\n| Method ID | 4 | 1 byte | uint8 | Attack method identifier |\\n| Num Targets | 5 | 1 byte | uint8 | Number of target entries |\\n| Num Options | 6 | 1 byte | uint8 | Number of option entries |\\n| Target Array | 7 | Variable | Binary | Array of target structures |\\n| Option Array | Variable | Variable | Binary | Array of option structures |\\n\\n#### Target Structure\\n\\n```\\n+------------------+------------------+--------+\\n| Target Address   | Target Netmask   | CIDR   |\\n| (sockaddr, 16B)  | (uint32, 4B)     | (1B)   |\\n+------------------+------------------+--------+\\n```\\n\\nEach target entry is 24 bytes total. The IP address is at offset 4 within the sockaddr structure.\\n\\n#### Option Structure\\n\\n```\\n+------------------+--------+\\n| Option Value     | Option |\\n| (pointer, 4B)    | ID     |\\n|                  | (1B)   |\\n+------------------+--------+\\n```\\n\\nEach option entry is 8 bytes total.\\n\\n### 3.3 Attack Method IDs\\n\\nThe `attack_init`